{"title":"2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the figure, the outer equilateral triangle has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the inner equilateral triangle has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the three trapezoids are congruent. What is the area of one of the trapezoids?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/4/e34c3dede3f2bef33570072537b95ad87b3894f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size((70)); draw((0,0)--(7.5,13)--(15,0)--(0,0)); draw((1.88,3.25)--(9.45,3.25)); draw((11.2,0)--(7.5,6.5)); draw((9.4,9.7)--(5.6,3.25)); [/asy]\" width=\"118\" height=\"102\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8528c604f00cf30e093b00e655bd6de60ea972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"349\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=43JZqmiUeLw\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=43JZqmiUeLw</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area outside the small triangle but inside the large triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2f79498733d3adf671f7818ffd0560dc67d622.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16-1=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />. This is equally distributed between the three trapezoids. Each trapezoid has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecfe04cb56640d10d6c8a37282cede0b5060133a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15/3 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"115\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can roughly see that 1 trapezoid = 5 triangles = 5 Area since 1 triangle is 1 area so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8d260a9a7112f522ac38809def477024784034c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=479\">https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=479</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span><